{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPKaKeLHvy8h5G46Lvqm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the change and wrote the report to `.ard/344/review-eng-review.md`. It has no blocking findings, only minor notes.\n\nThe planner, the tolerant lock parser, lock writing, the `CheckInitPath` change and the starter's protected paths match the issue and `plan.md`. The tests cover each planner case, including a hand-edited lock.\n\n- **Redundant check:** `internal/initcmd/initcmd.go:216` repeats an `if len(toWrite) == 0` check that the line above it already made.\n- **Stale runbook:** `docs/site/operations/gate-2-runbook.md:133` still says `ard init` refuses without `--force`. The change removes that flag and that refusal.\n- **Lock entries (info, no action):** files that already match the starter get no lock entry, so the lock stays empty until a file is created or updated. A file that goes stale later counts as edited, which is the safe direction.\n- **Lint:** `make lint` printed only a parse error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`, which the change did not touch. Nothing was reported on the changed files.\n- **Tests:** `go test -cover` passed for `internal/initcmd`, `internal/committer` and `internal/cli`. The planner branches are all covered. The uncovered lines are the `Marshal` error branch, `splitLines` for an empty file, and `Init` (the real dependency wiring)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":49877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"output_tokens":469,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f533c964-bf6e-4604-9e4a-a17dec7a44f6","uuid":"fdb6b7e2-9f8d-4eac